  "lean": {
    "statement": "∀ {E : Type u_1} [inst : NormedAddCommGroup E] [inst_1 : InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [inst_2 : FiniteDimensional ℝ E]\n  [inst_3 : MeasurableSpace E] [inst_4 : BorelSpace E] [inst_5 : CompleteSpace E] {U : E → ℝ} {α β : NNReal},\n  0 < α →\n    α ≤ β →\n      ContDiff ℝ 2 U →\n        (∀ (x v : E), ↑α * ‖v‖ ^ 2 ≤ ((fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ U) x) v) v ∧ ((fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ U) x) v) v ≤ ↑β * ‖v‖ ^ 2) →\n          ∀ (p : E),\n            gradient U p = 0 →\n              have μ := MeasureTheory.MeasureSpace.volume.tilted fun x => -U x;\n              MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure μ ∧\n                MeasureTheory.Integrable (fun x => Real.exp (-U x)) MeasureTheory.MeasureSpace.volume ∧\n                  0 < ∫ (x : E), Real.exp (-U x) ∧\n                    MeasureTheory.Integrable (fun x => ‖x - p‖ ^ 2) μ ∧\n                      MeasureTheory.Integrable (fun x => Inner.inner ℝ (x - p) (gradient U x)) μ ∧\n                        ∫ (x : E), Inner.inner ℝ (x - p) (gradient U x) ∂μ = ↑(Module.finrank ℝ E) ∧\n                          ∫ (x : E), ‖x - p‖ ^ 2 ∂μ ≤ ↑(Module.finrank ℝ E) / ↑α",
    "statement_sha256": "a85fb1b80a429c56689ae4ec762a46d1d89c03cd2047e6df206f0847b4da9d9c",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "NNReal is the type of nonnegative real numbers;the displayed upward coercion embeds them into the reals. Module.finrank is the finite real vector-space dimension. ContDiff R 2 means twice continuously Frechet differentiable. fderiv is the Frechet derivative and gradient is the genuine real inner-product gradient.",
      "MeasureTheory.MeasureSpace.volume is the canonical volume measure on the displayed finite-dimensional real inner-product space. Measure.tilted f is the exponential tilt of a measure by exp(f),normalized by its integral. The total definition of a tilt alone does not imply that its normalization integral is positive or finite,or that it is a probability measure;retain all displayed conclusions.",
      "MeasureTheory.Integrable means Bochner integrability. Displayed real integrals are Bochner integrals;their total Lean definition alone does not assert integrability. Inner.inner R is the real inner product. All quantifiers,inequalities,actual derivatives and measures retain their displayed order and values."
    ]
  },
